Phase A of the android-handoever.md plan (D1, finding F1): the device target moves out of the connectors table into a top-level 'android' config section {serial, tcp} — resolve_target was reading hidden global state through ConnectorManager with a silent DEFAULT_SERIAL fallback, violating ADR-022's connector contract and CLAUDE.md's no-hidden-config directive.

- config.rs: AndroidConfig {serial: Option, tcp: Option}, tcp overrides serial (same semantics the connector row had). NOT feature-gated — plain data, deserializes on every build, and Phase C kills the gates anyway.
- routes/android.rs: resolve_target(&Config) replaces resolve_target(db); with_device takes Arc<Config> via state.config() (cheap Arc clone per request, hot-swapped by apply_config). Fallback to DEFAULT_SERIAL now logged at debug (it fires per frame in the live-view loop — warn would spam); an unparseable android.tcp logs warn and falls through.
- setup.rs check_android_sdk probes the same config target (was db). New GET/POST /api/setup/android-target following the mcp-servers persistence pattern (save to xpressclaw.yaml + apply_config); POST validates tcp as SocketAddr, empty strings clear fields. This is the persistence surface the live-view gear panel uses (later commit).
- CLI F5 fixed: --serial lost its hardcoded emulator-5554 default; resolution is --tcp > --serial > workspace xpressclaw.yaml android.tcp > android.serial > DEFAULT_SERIAL, so CLI and agents can no longer silently address different devices. Config::load side-effect note: it writes a .yaml.bak on success (same as ).
- GOTCHA: Config is constructed field-by-field in 4 places (agents.rs x2, setup.rs upsert/delete mcp server) — every new top-level config field MUST be added to each or E0063. Compiler catches it, but if you add a config field, grep 'let new_config = ' first. My set_android_target uses (*state.config()).clone() + mutate instead — immune to this.
- Existing android connector DB rows are now dead (nothing reads them); Phase B deletes the connector type entirely. NOT migrated: a user who had set serial/tcp on the connector must re-enter it (fahreza's own dev box is the only known install).

Encoding gotcha for future sessions: do NOT round-trip Rust sources through PowerShell Get-Content|Set-Content — PS 5.1 reads UTF-8-no-BOM as ANSI and mangles em-dashes (had to git checkout android.rs and redo with the Edit tool).

Verified: cargo check -p cli with AND without --features android, 361 core tests pass.
